# Playwright MCP test generation rules (modivo.ua)

## Exploration
1. Always open https://modivo.ua with Playwright MCP and explore the real page BEFORE writing code. Never guess selectors.
2. The site shows a cookie consent banner. Every test must accept or close it first (put it in beforeEach).

## Code style
3. Language: JavaScript with @playwright/test. Match the import style used in playwright.config.js. No TypeScript.
4. Use baseURL from config: page.goto('/') instead of full URLs.
5. Selector priority: getByRole > getByLabel > getByPlaceholder > getByText > data-testid. No XPath, no auto-generated classes.
6. No hard waits; use web-first assertions.
7. No duplicated code: shared steps go into BasePage or a fixture.
8. Meaningful names; no magic strings — test data in tests/data/testData.js.
9. Test names follow "should <result> when <action>" and map to the test case ID (e.g. test('TC1: should show products when searching "кросівки"')).
10. Small methods (one responsibility), no commented-out code, no console.log.

## Page Object Model (mandatory)
11. All page interactions live in page classes under pages/. Test files contain NO selectors and NO page.locator/getBy calls.
12. One class per page or major component: BasePage, HomePage, SearchResultsPage, CategoryPage, ProductPage, CartPage.
13. BasePage holds shared logic: constructor(page), goto(path), acceptCookies(), header/search access.
14. Locators are defined once in the constructor as readonly properties (this.searchInput = page.getByRole(...)).
15. Page methods describe user actions in business language (search(query), addToCart(), selectFirstAvailableSize()) and return data or the next page object when navigation happens.
16. Assertions (expect) stay in test files, not in page classes. Exception: small waitFor* helpers that ensure the page is loaded.
17. File naming: PascalCase class, one class per file, e.g. pages/CartPage.js, exported with module.exports / export matching the project style.

## Test data and stability
18. Never hardcode specific product names or prices; the catalog changes. Select products dynamically (e.g. the first product in a listing).
19. The site is in Ukrainian. Assert on Ukrainian UI text or on URL/element state.
20. Each test is independent: no shared state between tests.
21. Every test must have at least one meaningful assertion on the outcome.

## Safety (live production site)
22. NEVER place a real order, submit payment, or register a real account.
23. Use obviously fake data for negative tests (e.g. test.invalid@example.com).

## Workflow
24. Save files to tests/cursor/ (Cursor) or tests/claude/ (Claude), named <feature>.spec.js.
25. After writing, run `npx playwright test <file>` and fix failures until the test passes (if you can run commands).
26. Do not modify playwright.config.js or other tests unless asked.